\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The residual edge as the other column}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{On the group of \ref{fdip-0126}, the free orbit gives
invariant functions of rank #{72}, and the residual orbit gives
a preserved space of rank #{12}. Environment constants scale
the sector sums and leave the one-edge matrix unchanged.}

\proof{
\p{\ref{fdip-0126} gives a free orbit of #{72} points. For that
orbit every stabilizer is trivial. \ref{fdip-0123} identifies
the invariant functions with the functions on the residual
quotient of the links. For one edge and a trivial stabilizer
that quotient is the group, which has #{72} elements.
\ref{fdip-012I} gives #{12} double cosets on the residual
orbit, and \ref{fdip-013H} gives a preserved space of that
rank. \ref{fdip-013A} multiplies each sector sum by its own
constant and leaves the one-edge matrix unchanged.}
}
